---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import InsightCard from '../components/InsightCard.astro';
import { articles } from '../data/articles';
---
<Layout title='Jennie Muso — Creative Portfolio' description='Selected websites by Jennie Muso: Veyra Cargo, Bayline Legal, JIN Restaurant, and Nacre Dental. Web design, UX and creative development.' current='home' styles={['fonts.css','styles.css','editorial.css','projects.css','reference-layout.css','refinements.css','final-touches.css','latest.css','insights.css','preview-fixes.css','iteration.css','content-updates.css']}>

      <section class="hero editorial-hero" id="work" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-meta"><span>Jennie Muso / digital designer & maker</span><span>Website design & development</span><span>Selected projects</span></div>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Muso<span>.designs</span></h1>
        <div class="editorial-gallery" aria-label="Featured projects">
          <figure class="project-mini mini-verya"><img src="/assets/case-studies/veyra-hero.webp" alt="Veyra cargo ship at the port" width="768" height="512"><figcaption><strong>Veyra Cargo</strong><span>Website design & development</span></figcaption><a class="mini-link" href="/work/veyra-cargo/" aria-label="View Veyra Cargo case study"><span class="project-view-cue">View work <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={17} /></span></a></figure>
          <figure class="project-mini mini-bayline"><img src="/assets/case-studies/bayline-hero.webp" alt="Bayline Legal professionals in conversation" width="768" height="512"><figcaption><strong>Bayline Legal</strong><span>Website design & development</span></figcaption><a class="mini-link" href="/work/bayline-legal/" aria-label="View Bayline Legal case study"><span class="project-view-cue">View work <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={17} /></span></a></figure>
          <figure class="project-mini mini-jin"><img src="/assets/case-studies/jin-hero.webp" alt="JIN restaurant dining scene" width="768" height="512"><figcaption><strong>JIN Restaurant</strong><span>Website design & development</span></figcaption><a class="mini-link" href="/work/jin-restaurant/" aria-label="View JIN Restaurant case study"><span class="project-view-cue">View work <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={17} /></span></a></figure>
          <figure class="project-mini mini-nacre"><img src="/assets/case-studies/nacre-hero.webp" alt="Portrait from the Nacre Dental website" width="768" height="512"><figcaption><strong>Nacre Dental</strong><span>Website design & development</span></figcaption><a class="mini-link" href="/work/nacre-dental/" aria-label="View Nacre Dental case study"><span class="project-view-cue">View work <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={17} /></span></a></figure>
          <p class="gallery-thesis">Design that looks closely.<br>Development that thinks ahead.</p>
          <a class="gallery-link" href="/work/">View more work <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={20} /></a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-foot"><span>Tools in my workflow: Astro / Cloudflare / Resend / GitHub</span></div>
      </section>

      <section class="solutions" id="solutions" aria-labelledby="solutions-title">
        <div class="solutions-intro"><h2 id="solutions-title">WHAT I MAKE<br>POSSIBLE<span>.</span></h2><p>Your website has to do more than impress for a second. It should help the right people understand you, trust you, and take the next step.</p></div>
        <div class="solutions-list">
          <details class="solution" open><summary><span>Web & app design</span><img src="/assets/service-web.jpg" alt="" width="630" height="623" loading="lazy"></summary><div class="solution-content"><div class="solution-copy"><p>A polished screen is only the beginning. I give your business a distinctive digital presence that expresses what makes it worth choosing, then carry that idea through every page and interaction.</p><p>We start with your audience and the job the experience needs to do. From there, I shape the art direction, layout, typography, responsive screens, and the details that make the whole thing feel unmistakably yours.</p><span>For clients who want a digital presence with a point of view.</span></div></div></details>
          <details class="solution"><summary><span>UX design</span><img src="/assets/service-ux.jpg" alt="" width="630" height="623" loading="lazy"></summary><div class="solution-content"><div class="solution-copy"><p>People should not have to work to understand your website. I map what visitors need, organise the content around their questions, and make important actions easy to find.</p><p>That means clearer navigation, stronger page flow, useful calls to action, and careful attention to mobile, accessibility, and the little moments where confidence is won or lost.</p><span>For clients who need visitors to move from curiosity to action.</span></div></div></details>
          <details class="solution"><summary><span>No-code building</span><img src="/assets/service-nocode.jpg" alt="" width="630" height="624" loading="lazy"></summary><div class="solution-content"><div class="solution-copy"><p>Some ideas need a fast, flexible route to launch. I use visual building tools when they fit the brief, turning the approved design into a working website without adding technical complexity you do not need.</p><p>The result is considered from both sides: an experience your visitors can use and a site you can manage. The tool is chosen around the project, not the other way around.</p><span>For clients who want to launch and keep moving.</span></div></div></details>
          <details class="solution"><summary><span>Vibe coding</span><img src="/assets/service-code.jpg" alt="" width="630" height="624" loading="lazy"></summary><div class="solution-content"><div class="solution-copy"><p>When a project needs custom behaviour or more room to grow, I take it beyond a static mockup. I use Codex and Claude Code as development collaborators while keeping the concept, decisions, and quality bar firmly human-led.</p><p>Depending on the brief, that can mean Astro or React for the experience, Cloudflare for hosting or infrastructure, Resend for email, and GitHub for versioned delivery. You get a thoughtful design and a practical build in one connected process.</p><span>For clients who need something tailored, functional, and ready to evolve.</span></div></div></details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="manifesto about-story" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title"><div class="about-top"><span class="about-photo"><img src="/assets/jennie-portrait-preview.jpg" alt="Portrait of Jennie Muso at a desk with a tablet" width="1086" height="1448" loading="lazy"></span><span class="about-name">Jennie Muso<br>Founder & Designer</span></div><h2 id="about-title" class="about-statement" aria-label="I design with intention, bringing structure and expression together to make websites that speak clearly and feel unmistakably yours. I bring curiosity to every brief, making the complex feel clear, considered, and worth remembering."><span class="reveal-word revealed">I</span> <span class="reveal-word revealed">design</span> <span class="reveal-word revealed">with</span> <span class="reveal-word revealed">intention,</span> <span class="reveal-word">bringing</span> <span class="reveal-word">structure</span> <span class="reveal-word">and</span> <span class="reveal-word">expression</span> <span class="reveal-word">together</span> <span class="reveal-word">to</span> <span class="reveal-word">make</span> <span class="reveal-word">websites</span> <span class="reveal-word">that</span> <span class="reveal-word">speak</span> <span class="reveal-word">clearly</span> <span class="reveal-word">and</span> <span class="reveal-word">feel</span> <span class="reveal-word">unmistakably</span> <span class="reveal-word">yours.</span> <span class="reveal-word">I</span> <span class="reveal-word">bring</span> <span class="reveal-word">curiosity</span> <span class="reveal-word">to</span> <span class="reveal-word">every</span> <span class="reveal-word">brief,</span> <span class="reveal-word">making</span> <span class="reveal-word">the</span> <span class="reveal-word">complex</span> <span class="reveal-word">feel</span> <span class="reveal-word">clear,</span> <span class="reveal-word">considered,</span> <span class="reveal-word">and</span> <span class="reveal-word">worth</span> <span class="reveal-word">remembering.</span></h2><a class="text-link about-link" href="/contact/">Work with me <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={20} /></a></section>

      <section class="insights" id="insights" aria-labelledby="insights-title"><div class="insights-head"><h2 id="insights-title">THINGS I’VE<br>BEEN THINKING<br>ABOUT<span>.</span></h2><p>Notes on building digital experiences that look good, make sense, and do their job.</p></div><div class="insights-grid">
        {articles.map((article, index) => <InsightCard article={article} featured={index === 0} />)}
      </div><a class="text-link insights-more" href="/blog/">View more insights <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={20} /></a></section>

      <section class="shop-teaser" id="shop" aria-labelledby="shop-title"><h2 id="shop-title">GOOD THINGS<br>TAKE SHAPE<span>.</span></h2><div class="shop-bottom"><p>A small collection of website templates and components is on its way.</p><a class="text-link shop-link" href="/shop/">Explore the shop <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={20} /></a></div></section>
      <section class="contact" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><div class="contact-main"><div class="contact-copy"><p>Have a project in mind?</p><h2 id="contact-title">LET’S MAKE<br>SOMETHING<br>MATTER<span>.</span></h2></div><div class="contact-eyes" aria-hidden="true"><span class="contact-eye"><span class="contact-pupil"></span></span><span class="contact-eye"><span class="contact-pupil"></span></span></div></div><a href="/contact/" class="contact-link">Start a conversation <Icon name="ArrowUpRight" size={20} /></a></section>

</Layout>
